Ruth Zuniga wants justice that's been a  long time coming like 300,000 other  women in Peru she was a victim of forced  sterilization in the nineties the then  President of Peru Alberto Fujimori  initiated a program to combat poverty  and encourage birth control the  sterilizations were framed as voluntary  but the women forced to have them say  they were anything but ruth is trying to  get other victims to break their silence  and demand compensation can she  convinced these women to stand up for  their rights  mommy Taiwan China awesome a mutator  Scalia today Ruth is visiting a village  in Peru's Cusco region she's trying to  identify and register women who were  forcibly sterilized in a government  program that lasted for two decades  you've got to hand in a report you've  got to tell us what they did to you I've  done that myself we have to stick  together  women who register will get financial  compensation and help with physical and  psychological problems it's humiliating  it's nothing to be ashamed of we've got  to stay strong sterilization changed  everything  I can't work as hard in the fields as  they used to because of the pain my  husband doesn't understand he thinks I'm  lazy  most of the sterilizations were carried  out in rural areas in poor indigenous  communities many of them could neither  read nor write they had no idea what was  going to happen when they arrived at the  doctor's office that's why many of the  victims are reluctant to register so far  500 women in the Cusco region have  signed up and today Ruth manages to  convince a few more to do so  Mondays already full so sign up for  Tuesday I'll be there the women have to  travel to the regional capital cuzco to  register ruth will go with them to give  them support but it's an election year  and that complicates the situation the  leading candidate for president is the  daughter of former president Alberto  Fujimori who's serving a 25 year prison  sentence for crimes including corruption  the forced sterilization program began  during his administration Ruth wants to  make sure that the women do actually  join the program they're worried some  think the government is spying on them  they're afraid that if they register  they'll get into trouble  Ruth and her husband farmer plot of land  near the village of limbo Tambo about 60  kilometers west of Cusco  we've run out of beans so we'll just  have to do without I'll throw in some  herbs I'm going down to the village  I'll see whether anyone has a job for me  today feed first and bring some water  back with you  Ruth receives no financial compensation  for her work she says she's simply  trying to win respect for the  sterilization victims in the old days a  new wife had to peel potatoes in front  of her mother-in-law you started out  with really small potatoes so you could  prove that you could peel them once you  did you were accepted as a woman thank  God it's not like that anymore  in a manual it was in 1999 February the  10th a nurse asked Ruth to bring her  youngest child to the Medical Center for  a free examination something didn't seem  right so I my husband and my child tried  to get out of there the door was locked  I tried to make it look like I was going  to the restroom but the door wouldn't  open  I could hear women screaming in rooms  nearby I was really scared  they took off my clothes put me in a  green smock and lifted me onto a bed I  asked the nurse why they were doing this  to me they told me they wanted to  examine my child not me they tricked me  she said you've already got four kids  how many more do you want  it's just a small incision it's for your  own good they cut me open  there was a lot of blood the surgeon  said hold her down the nurses grabbed my  arms and head and they tied my feet and  hands to the bed they kept holding my  head down I flashed around I don't know  how it happened but I managed to pull  off the doctors surgical mask  Vega chuckle me man sick Paulo Brazil  amis action / SMS me no magic words no  play staccato through la máscara I saw  right away it was Washington Ortiz many  of the local women say that it was Ortiz  who sterilized them without their  consent  there's been no official investigation  of these cases Ortiz has made no public  comment on them Ruth's husband was not  able to defend or protect his wife at  the time we had no idea what the doctors  were going to do to her how did they  come up with this idea we didn't even  know what sterilization was I didn't  know and neither did my wife we didn't  have a clue so did you sign anything  absolutely not this is the medical  center in the town of anta many of the  local women were sterilized here when  the center first opened president  fujimori himself took part in the  dedication ceremony Washington Ortiz who  carried out so many of the sterilization  procedures still works here he refuses  to appear before our camera and pretends  he's not there many women are afraid of  being treated at the center we finally  found a doctor who was willing to  discuss the sterilization program dr.  Raul Salas carry on is the chairman of  the Regional Medical Council at that  time there were guidelines on how many  women should be sterilized every month  and every year nationwide the numbers  were set by the federal government if a  doctor didn't meet the quota he'd be  moved to another job former president  fujimori denies he knew anything about  the sterilization program his daughter  the presidential candidate puts the  responsibility squarely on the  individual doctors who were involved  now Ruth is on her way to cruise pitar  another village near Cusco lots of  people have come here today to see a  bullfight  perhaps Ruth will be able to sign up  some more women for the compensation  program she meets one of her fellow  volunteers how many women still haven't  signed up 45 I've been talking to some  of them about it Ruth wants to meet as  many of these women as she can who has  signed up a lot of us can't remember  when the procedure took place and some  of the women can't read or write how old  were you at the time and how old are you  now try to remember it's important and  don't forget to bring some official ID  but Ruth knows from experience that not  many of these women will actually  register for the program  on the weekend Ruth's family gathers at  her home her four children now live in  cusco but they visit their parents often  Ruth and Eduardo couldn't imagine a life  without their children Ruth doesn't want  her daughter's to experience what she  went through her goal is to convince the  sterilization victims to break their  silence and get the help they need  you
 

